{"Injecting synthetic 'refresh_token' value when absent masks protocol violations and can lead to storing invalid token state - OAuth providers expect existing refresh_token to be reused": 0.9229045510292053, "Zod schema definition is invalid - Zod doesn't support computed property names like [z.string().toString()] in object schemas, making schema check ineffective": 0.902245819568634, "Webhook handler should explicitly enforce POST-only requests to reduce attack surface by rejecting unintended HTTP methods": 0.5644537210464478, "Webhook authentication relies solely on static header comparison without HMAC signature verification, timestamp validation, or replay protection - intercepted requests can be replayed indefinitely": 0.875042200088501, "Schema validation errors will throw and result in a 500 response instead of catching validation errors and returning 400 with safe error messages": 0.9671962261199951, "Decryption and JSON parsing can throw on malformed input (wrong encryption key, corrupted ciphertext, or invalid JSON) without error handling": 0.9945952296257019, "No validation of the decrypted keys structure before storing - could store malformed credential data": 0.7316650152206421, "findFirst + update/create pattern is vulnerable to race conditions if multiple webhook deliveries arrive concurrently for the same user+app, potentially creating duplicate credentials": 0.9473185539245605, "Delegated refresh request has no timeout - if external endpoint hangs, refresh will block indefinitely": 0.9340283870697021, "Delegated refresh request doesn't include any signature or shared secret to prove caller identity": 0.8677804470062256, "Delegated refresh has no fallback to refreshFunction() if endpoint returns non-2xx or is unreachable": 0.9096986651420593, "Delegated refresh has no error handling for network errors which will propagate uncaught": 0.829867959022522, "APP_CREDENTIAL_SHARING_ENABLED only checks for webhook secret and encryption key but refresh delegation also requires CALCOM_CREDENTIAL_SYNC_ENDPOINT, creating ambiguous partial-enabled state": 0.8511940836906433, "Salesforce integration is not using refreshOAuthTokens utility like other integrations, so it won't support credential sync delegation when enabled": 0.8101246356964111, "parseRefreshTokenResponse is passed googleCredentials which has already been mutated with new tokens instead of the raw token response, meaning schema validation checks the wrong object": 0.9034785032272339}